+#### Max Consecutive Losses
+
+`MaxConsecutiveLosses` looks at the most recently closed trades for a pair. If the last `trade_limit` trades in a row all resulted in a loss (negative profit), that pair will be locked for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`) - any single winning trade breaks the streak.
+
+Unless `only_per_pair` is set to true, the same check is also applied across all pairs combined: if the last `trade_limit` trades closed anywhere - regardless of pair - were all losses, trading is paused for every pair until the cooldown expires.
+
+Unlike `StoplossGuard`, this only cares about the streak of consecutive losses, not the total number of losses within a time window, and it does not require the exit to have been triggered by a stoploss - any losing trade counts. This protection ignores `lookback_period`, since it only evaluates the trailing streak of closed trades, however long ago they closed.
+
+The below example stops trading a pair (and, since `only_per_pair` is not set, all pairs) for 6 candles after 3 consecutive losing trades.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "trade_limit": 3,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 6,
+            "only_per_pair": False,
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
 ### Full example of Protections
 
 All protections can be combined at will, also with different parameters, creating a increasing wall for under-performing pairs.
